    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The positive integer $N$ is the smallest one whose digits add to 41. What is the sum of the digits of $N+2021$?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "10"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "12"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "16"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "2021"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "4042"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Build the smallest number",
        "body": "Four digits give at most $4\\times9=36<41$, so $N$ has at least 5 digits. To make $N$ as small as possible, use exactly 5 digits and make the first digit as small as possible, so the other four digits are all 9 (sum 36). The first digit is then $41-36=5$, so $N=59\\,999$.\n\n$N+2021=59\\,999+2021=62\\,020$, and its digit sum is $6+2+0+2+0=10$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 10**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Use a shortcut",
        "body": "Once $N=59\\,999=60\\,000-1$ is found, $N+2021=60\\,000+2020=62\\,020$ without any carrying, and the digit sum is $6+2+2=10$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 10**"
      }
    ],
