    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Lewis and Geraint left Acaster to travel to Beetown at the same time. Lewis stopped for an hour in Beetown and then drove back towards Acaster. He drove at a constant 70 km/h. He met Geraint, who was cycling at a constant 30 km/h, 105 km from Beetown. How far is it from Acaster to Beetown?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "315 km"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "300 km"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "250 km"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "210 km"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "180 km"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Equate the travelling times",
        "body": "Let the distance be $x$ km. When they meet, Geraint has cycled $x-105$ km, taking $\\frac{x-105}{30}$ hours. Lewis has driven to Beetown and $105$ km back, so $x+105$ km, taking $\\frac{x+105}{70}$ hours of driving plus 1 hour of stopping. They travelled for the same total time:\n\n$$\\frac{x-105}{30}=\\frac{x+105}{70}+1.$$\n\nMultiplying by 210: $7(x-105)=3(x+105)+210$, so $4x=1260$ and $x=315$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 315 km**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Check the answer",
        "body": "For $x=315$: Geraint has cycled $210$ km, which takes $210\\div30=7$ hours. Lewis has driven $315+105=420$ km, which takes $420\\div70=6$ hours, plus 1 hour stopped, so also 7 hours. The equation above is linear, so this is the only solution.\n\n**Answer: (A) 315 km**"
      }
    ],
